.TH IFTOP-JSON 8 "October 2026" "iftop-json" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
iftop-json \- write bandwidth usage per connection as JSON
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B iftop-json
[\fB\-hnNpPl\fR] [\fB\-i\fR \fIinterface\fR] [\fB\-f\fR \fIfilter code\fR]
[\fB\-F\fR \fInet/mask\fR] [\fB\-G\fR \fInet6/mask6\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fIconfig file\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B iftop-json
listens to network traffic on an interface and works out the bandwidth used
by each pair of hosts, like
.BR iftop (8),
but has no interactive display. Every two seconds it writes one line of JSON
to standard output, until it is terminated.
.PP
Each line is an object with these keys:
.TP
.B timestamp
Unix time of the sample.
.TP
.B interface
The interface being watched.
.TP
.B connections
A list with one object per connection:
.BR src " and " dst
(each with
.B addr
\(em the numeric address,
.B host
\(em the resolved name or null,
.BR port " and " service ),
.B protocol
(IP protocol number),
.BR sent_rate " and " recv_rate
(bytes per second averaged over 2, 10 and 40 seconds), and
.BR total_sent " and " total_recv
(bytes).
.TP
.B totals
The same rates and totals for the whole interface, plus
.BR peak_sent_rate ", " peak_recv_rate " and " peak_total_rate .
.PP
Capturing packets requires root or the capabilities CAP_NET_RAW and
CAP_NET_ADMIN.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h
Print a summary of the options.
.TP
.B \-n
Don't look up host names.
.TP
.B \-N
Don't convert port numbers to service names.
.TP
.B \-p
Run in promiscuous mode, so traffic between other hosts is counted too.
.TP
.B \-P
Report ports as well as hosts. Without it, connections are only told apart by
their hosts.
.TP
.B \-l
Include link-local IPv6 traffic.
.TP
.BI \-i " interface"
Listen on the named interface. By default the first running interface is
used.
.TP
.BI \-f " filter code"
Only count packets matching the pcap filter, see
.BR pcap-filter (7).
.TP
.BI \-F " net/mask"
Report traffic flowing in and out of this IPv4 network.
.TP
.BI \-G " net6/mask6"
Report traffic flowing in and out of this IPv6 network.
.TP
.BI \-c " config file"
Read this configuration file instead of
.IR ~/.iftoprc .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR iftop (8),
.BR iftop-web-user (8),
.BR pcap-filter (7)
